 },
 "evaluation_criteria": "Paired relative differences per seed, mean and two-sided 95% Student-t CI; seed means for fractions and counts.",
 "sample_size": "5 seeds x 5 conditions x 6 schedulers = 150 runs (each ~400 jobs).",
 "randomization": "Job streams drawn per (condition, seed) and shared by all schedulers.",
 "measurement_boundary": "Simulated facility electricity (IT / conversion efficiency, pumps, dry-cooler fans, chiller) of 32 GPUs; jobs counted on time if finished by their deadline; unfinished jobs at the end of the drain count as not on time.",
 "known_limitations": "Synthetic jobs and illustrative accelerator types; lumped junction model; instant supply (no plant lag); no migration; communication costs are stated constants; thermal-credit parameters were set by hand, not tuned; one topology size.",
 "known_confounders": [
  "thermal_credit may lower clocks, which changes IT energy as well as temperatures; the thermal_placement ablation separates this"
 ],
 "disclosure": "Before registration, exploratory runs while building the simulator: one 1-h run (2x2 nodes, series pairs, spread 0.6, rack limit 9 kW, load 0.8, supply 35 C, seed 1) gave thermal_credit ~11% lower energy per job, 60% fewer chip-seconds above target and a slightly lower on-time fraction (0.977 vs 0.991) than least_loaded; unit-test runs. No E018 cell was run before registration.",
